speechtext:
There is no unanimous consent.

It is my duty, pursuant to Standing Order 38, to inform the House that the questions to be raised tonight at the time of adjournment are as follows: the hon. member for York West-Airports; the hon. member for Skeena- Fisheries; the hon. member for Halifax-Port of Halifax;
the hon. member for Don Valley East-Manufacturing industry; and the hon. member for St. Boniface-Education.
